# popupHeight is raised from the shell's own default of 400 to 900 to fix a determinism
# defect (see harness/shots/determinism.py): the launcher's actual popup height is
# max(popupHeight, the popup content's own implicit height), and the content's implicit
# height varies by a few logical pixels from boot to boot (same signed image, same
# steps - the exact QML-internal cause was not identified further, but confirmed narrow:
# unaffected by restarting plasmashell or reopening the popup within one boot, and
# unaffected by waiting longer before the first open; only a fresh boot reproduces it,
# and the variance is bigger, or hit more often, once the desktop-empty state's own
# reset/settle cycle runs before the popup is opened - a smaller margin (450) that
# removed the flip in isolation still failed intermittently in the full state sequence).
# When the content's height exceeds popupHeight on one boot but not another, the popup's
# overall height differs by that amount and shifts the bottom footer bar (the
# Applications/Places tabs and the power buttons) by a few pixels, which two-boot
# determinism checking then reports as ~17,000 differing pixels. 900 exceeds the
# available screen height above the panel, so the popup is instead clamped to the
# largest size that fits on screen - a fixed value driven by screen geometry, not by the
# content's variable implicit height, which is robust to that variance regardless of its
# size. The trade-off (accepted deliberately): the popup now shows more empty space below
# the favourites grid than the shell's own default of 400 did; a human reviewing the
# golden image can revisit this if a tighter layout is wanted later.
[Containments][2][Applets][3][Configuration]
popupHeight=900
popupWidth=560

[Containments][2][Applets][3][Configuration][General]
favorites=systemsettings.desktop,org.kde.dolphin.desktop,org.kde.konsole.desktop

